-- title:
--   Component intersection on the resolved model: finite, degree the edge count
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0\ne 0$ and a prime $p$ with $p\nmid N_0$, a model package $\mathfrak P$ of level $\Gamma_0(N_0p)$ over the base ring `DRLevel.R p`, a commutative ring $O$ with a ring homomorphism $\rho_O:\,$`DRLevel.R p`$\to O$, and an algebraically closed field $\kappa$ of characteristic $p$ with a ring homomorphism $O\to\kappa$. Let $R$ be a `DRResolvedModelPackageLevel` for these data: a scheme $Y$, proper, flat and integral over $\operatorname{Spec} O$, regular of stalk dimension at most $2$ away from the locus where $p$ is invertible, isomorphic to the Deligne–Rapoport model on the smooth locus and over the $p$-invertible locus, equipped with a finite type `R.node` of crossing points matched with the crossings of the two level-$N_0$ fibre copies, widths `R.width` $\ge 1$, and a family of invertible ideal sheaf data `R.comp v` with integral closed subschemes, supported in the fibre over $p$ and with $\prod_v$ `R.comp v` generated by $p$, indexed by $v\in$ `X0MqComponents R.width` $=\mathrm{Fin}\,2\oplus\coprod_{n}\mathrm{Fin}(\mathrm{width}(n)-1)$; here `chainPos R.width n d` is the $d$-th position on the chain over the node $n$, namely $\mathrm{inl}\,0$ for $d=0$, the intermediate component $(n,d-1)$ for $0<d<\mathrm{width}(n)$, and $\mathrm{inl}\,1$ otherwise, and `R.edgePt n d` is the corresponding intersection point of $Y$. Let $v\ne w$ be two component indices, $k$ a field, and $y:$ `(R.comp w).subscheme` $\to\operatorname{Spec} k$ a morphism from the closed subscheme cut out by `R.comp w`. Assume that for every node $n$ and every $d<\mathrm{width}(n)$ such that the unordered pair $\{$`chainPos R.width n d`$,\,$`chainPos R.width n (d+1)`$\}$ equals $\{v,w\}$ (written as the two-case disjunction) there is a section $s:\operatorname{Spec} k\to$ `(R.comp w).subscheme` with $y\circ s=\mathrm{id}$ whose composite with the closed immersion `(R.comp w).subschemeι` has `R.edgePt n d` in the range of its underlying map. Then the closed subscheme of `(R.comp w).subscheme` defined by the pullback ideal sheaf data `(R.comp v).comap (R.comp w).subschemeι`, composed into $\operatorname{Spec} k$ via its closed immersion followed by $y$, is a finite morphism, and for every point $t$ of $\operatorname{Spec} k$ the invariant `finrank` of this morphism at $t$ equals the cardinality of the set of pairs $(n,d)$ with $d<\mathrm{width}(n)$ whose associated chain edge joins $v$ and $w$, i.e. satisfies the same disjunction.
--
--   This is the local intersection computation on the resolved (regular) model of $X_0(N_0p)$: the scheme-theoretic intersection of the component $C_v$ with the component $C_w$ is finite over the residue field $k$ and has degree the number of edges joining $v$ and $w$ in the subdivided dual graph of the special fibre. It feeds the Euler-characteristic and degree computations for line bundles on the special fibre of the model.
